course: dictionary
lesson: 3693
title: Two names, one light
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A flashlight is a small electric light that you hold in your hand. It runs on batteries. In the UK, Ireland and Australia, people usually call the same thing a torch.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «In a power cut, use a torch (flashlight) rather than candles.» The power is off, so you need a light that does not need the mains. The brackets tell you that torch and flashlight are two names for the same thing.
explain: Flashlight can also mean the flash on a camera, so check the words around it. «Shine a flashlight» and «a flashlight beam» point to the hand-held light. If the sentence is about taking a photo, it may mean the camera flash. Always ask: does my meaning still make sense in the sentence?
fact: A flashlight is a small electric light you hold in your hand, powered by batteries.
fact: In the UK, Ireland and Australia, a flashlight is usually called a torch.
fact: «Shine a flashlight» and «a flashlight beam» both refer to the light the flashlight gives out.
fact: Flashlight can also mean the flash on a camera.
fact: People keep a flashlight for power cuts, camping and emergencies.
exercise: «In a power cut, use a torch (flashlight) rather than candles.» What is a flashlight? | A kind of fridge | A type of camera | *A small electric light you hold in your hand | A candle in a glass jar
exercise: Ella's cousin in New York says she packed a flashlight for camping. What did she pack? | A noisy alarm bell | *A small electric light you hold in your hand | A bright sun in the sky
exercise: «Switch on the flashlight.» What does this phrase mean? | *Turn the light on | Drop the flashlight in the sea | Put the flashlight in a bag
test: In a power cut, what does the sentence say to use rather than candles? | A pile of books | A birthday cake | A hot bath | *A flashlight
test: Which sentence uses flashlight to mean the flash on a camera? | «He packed a flashlight for the camping trip.» | «The flashlight beam lit up the cave.» | *«The photo was too dark, so she turned on the flashlight.»
exam: Why does the lesson write «torch (flashlight)» with brackets? | To show a torch is bigger than a flashlight | To show the flashlight is broken | To show torches are made of wood | *To show they are two names for the same thing
